                                                              "date":  "2026-09-22",
                                                              "imageUrl":  null,
                                                              "summary":  "Santoli describes months of \u0027bend-don\u0027t-break\u0027 market action that kept the S\u0026P 500 near record highs despite headwinds from higher oil prices, rising rates, and softening consumer cyclicals. He notes semiconductor stocks and mega-cap tech platforms were recovering as fears of AI capex overbuilding faded. Using a rip-current analogy, he frames the market as maneuvering cautiously sideways rather than fighting directly against macro headwinds. The piece questions whether a rally concentrated in AI implementers signals a genuine breakout from summer stagnation.",
