                                                                                "summary":  "Damodaran argues that venture capital\u0027s doctrine of scaling at all costs ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ã‚Â¬ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã‚Â prioritizing revenue growth over unit economics ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ã‚Â¬ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã‚Â has become structurally broken. He contends that not every business benefits from aggressive expansion, and that market structure, competitive dynamics, and unit economics must determine whether scaling makes sense. The influx of public equity money into private markets has amplified pressure on founders to grow revenue regardless of profitability, distorting incentives. Companies going public today are larger, less profitable, and priced at far higher multiples than historical cohorts, raising long-term return risk.",
