                                                                                "summary":  "Josh Brown, drawing on commentary from tech analyst Alex Kantrowitz, argues that current debates about AI infrastructure overbuilding fundamentally misread the demand trajectory. The piece contends that the real compute demand ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ã‚Â¬ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã‚Â driven by a future world of a billion people each running personal AI assistants, autonomous agents, and robots ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ã‚Â¬ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã‚Â dwarfs anything currently deployed. Industry leaders are not building for today\u0027s chatbot market; they are laying groundwork for an agentic AI era that will require orders of magnitude more infrastructure. Current AI capex, in this framing, is not a bubble but a down payment.",
