                                                                                "summary":  "Josh Brown profiles Ron Baron of Baron Capital and the disciplined long-term conviction investing that has made his funds among the best-performing actively managed mutual funds since 2003. The piece highlights Baron\u0027s early and outsized bets on Tesla ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ã‚Â¬ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã‚Â purchased at a split-adjusted $14 per share in 2014 ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ã‚Â¬ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã‚Â and SpaceX, both of which generated extraordinary returns that compounded across the fund. Brown uses Baron as a case study for the virtues of ignoring short-term media criticism and maintaining conviction in high-quality, long-duration growth businesses. The total return figure of over $60 billion returned to investors is presented as validation of the strategy.",
